#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Enable or Disable LDAP referrals.  If disabled, it may increase the speed of searches."
msgstr "Kunna ko Kashe turawar LDAP. Idan an kashe, hakan na iya ƙara saurin bincike."

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "Yanayi"

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Mode which cacti will attempt to authenticate against the LDAP server.<blockquote><i>No Searching</i> - No Distinguished Name (DN) searching occurs, just attempt to bind with the provided Distinguished Name (DN) format.<br><br><i>Anonymous Searching</i> - Attempts to search for username against LDAP directory via anonymous binding to locate the user's Distinguished Name (DN).<br><br><i>Specific Searching</i> - Attempts search for username against LDAP directory via Specific Distinguished Name (DN) and Specific Password for binding to locate the user's Distinguished Name (DN).<br><br><i>One-Time Passwords (OTP/MFA)</i> - Cacti binds the user's password only once, during final authentication.  <i>No Searching</i> performs no directory lookup and binds directly using the Distinguished Name (DN) template, so it is safe for OTP when the DN template alone identifies the user.  When a directory lookup is required to resolve the DN, use <i>Specific Searching</i> with a dedicated service account (or <i>Anonymous Searching</i> where the directory permits it) so the lookup never consumes the user's single-use code.  For resilient OTP deployments use a single DNS load balancer name in the Server(s) field rather than a space delimited multi-server list, which would re-attempt the bind with an already-consumed one-time password."
msgstr "Yanayin da Cacti zai yi ƙoƙarin tantancewa da uwar garken LDAP.<blockquote><i>Babu Bincike</i> - Ba a yin binciken Distinguished Name (DN), kawai a yi ƙoƙarin haɗawa (bind) da tsarin Distinguished Name (DN) da aka bayar.<br><br><i>Bincike Ba Tare da Suna Ba</i> - Yana ƙoƙarin nemo sunan mai amfani a cikin kundin adireshi na LDAP ta hanyar haɗawa ba tare da suna ba domin gano Distinguished Name (DN) na mai amfani.<br><br><i>Takamaiman Bincike</i> - Yana ƙoƙarin nemo sunan mai amfani a cikin kundin adireshi na LDAP ta hanyar Takamaiman Distinguished Name (DN) da Takamaiman Kalmar Sirri don haɗawa domin gano Distinguished Name (DN) na mai amfani.<br><br><i>Kalmomin Sirri na Lokaci Guda (OTP/MFA)</i> - Cacti yana haɗa kalmar sirrin mai amfani sau ɗaya tak, yayin tantancewar ƙarshe. <i>Babu Bincike</i> ba ya yin binciken kundin adireshi kuma yana haɗawa kai tsaye ta amfani da samfurin Distinguished Name (DN), don haka yana da aminci ga OTP idan samfurin DN kaɗai ya isa gano mai amfani. Idan ana buƙatar binciken kundin adireshi don gano DN, yi amfani da <i>Takamaiman Bincike</i> tare da asusun sabis na musamman (ko <i>Bincike Ba Tare da Suna Ba</i> inda kundin adireshi ya yarda da hakan) domin binciken kada ya ƙare lambar amfani sau ɗaya ta mai amfani. Don ingantaccen tsarin OTP mai juriya, yi amfani da sunan DNS load balancer guda ɗaya a filin Uwar Garke (Server(s)) maimakon jerin sabobin da aka raba da sarari, wanda zai sake ƙoƙarin haɗawa da kalmar sirri ta lokaci guda da aka riga aka yi amfani da ita."

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Distinguished Name (DN)"
msgstr "Fitaccen Suna (DN)"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "The \"Distinguished Name\" syntax, applicable for both OpenLDAP and Windows AD configurations, offers flexibility in defining user identity. For OpenLDAP, the format follows this structure: <i>\"uid=&lt;username&gt;,ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>. Windows AD provides an alternative syntax: <i>\"&lt;username&gt;@win2kdomain.local\"</i>, commonly known as \"userPrincipalName (UPN)\". In this context, \"&lt;username&gt;\" represents the specific username provided during the login prompt. This is particularly pertinent when operating in \"No Searching\" mode, or \"Require Group Membership\" enabled."
msgstr "Tsarin \"Fitaccen Suna\", wanda ya dace da saitunan OpenLDAP da Windows AD duka, yana ba da sauƙi wajen ayyana asalin mai amfani. Ga OpenLDAP, tsarin yana bin wannan tsari: <i>\"uid=&lt;username&gt;,ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>. Windows AD yana ba da wani tsari na daban: <i>\"&lt;username&gt;@win2kdomain.local\"</i>, wanda aka fi sani da \"userPrincipalName (UPN)\". A cikin wannan mahallin, \"&lt;username&gt;\" yana wakiltar takamaiman sunan mai amfani da aka bayar yayin shiga. Wannan yana da muhimmanci musamman idan ana aiki a yanayin \"Ba Bincike\", ko idan an kunna \"Buƙatar Kasancewa Mamba a Ƙungiya\"."

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Require Group Membership"
msgstr "Buƙatar Kasancewa Mamba a Rukuni"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Require user to be member of group to authenticate. Group settings must be set for this to work, enabling without proper group settings will cause authentication failure."
msgstr "Yana buƙatar mai amfani ya kasance mamba na rukuni don a tantance shi. Dole ne a saita saitunan rukuni domin wannan ya yi aiki, kunnawa ba tare da ingantattun saitunan rukuni ba zai haifar da gazawar tantancewa."

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "LDAP Group Settings"
msgstr "Saitunan Rukunin LDAP"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Group Distinguished Name (DN)"
msgstr "Fitaccen Sunan Ƙungiya (DN)"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Distinguished Name of the group that user must have membership."
msgstr "Distinguished Name na rukunin da dole ne mai amfani ya kasance mamba a cikinsa."

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Group Member Attribute"
msgstr "Siffar Mamban Ƙungiya"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "This refers to the specific attribute within the LDAP directory that holds the usernames of group members. It is crucial to ensure that the attribute value aligns with the configuration specified in the \"Distinguished Name\" or that the actual attribute value is searchable using the settings outlined in the \"Distinguished Name\"."
msgstr "Wannan yana nufin takamaiman siffa a cikin kundin LDAP wadda ke ɗauke da sunayen masu amfani na mambobin ƙungiya. Yana da matuƙar muhimmanci a tabbatar cewa ƙimar siffar ta yi daidai da saitin da aka ayyana a cikin \"Fitaccen Suna\" ko kuma ana iya bincika ainihin ƙimar siffar ta amfani da saitunan da aka zayyana a cikin \"Fitaccen Suna\"."

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Group Member Type"
msgstr "Nau'in Mamban Ƙungiya"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Defines if users use full Distinguished Name or just Username in the defined Group Member Attribute."
msgstr "Yana ayyana ko masu amfani suna amfani da cikakken Fitaccen Suna ko Sunan Mai Amfani kawai a cikin Siffar Mamban Ƙungiya da aka ayyana."

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Distinguished Name"
msgstr "Sunan Tantancewa (Distinguished Name)"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "LDAP Specific Search Settings"
msgstr "Takamaiman Saitunan Bincike na LDAP"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Search Base"
msgstr "Tushen Bincike"

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Search base for searching the LDAP directory, such as <i>'dc=win2kdomain,dc=local'</i> or <i>'ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local'</i>."
msgstr "Tushen bincike don bincika kundin adireshi na LDAP, kamar <i>'dc=win2kdomain,dc=local'</i> ko <i>'ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local'</i>."

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Search Filter"
msgstr "Matacin Bincike"

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Search filter to use to locate the user in the LDAP directory, such as for windows: <i>'(&amp;(objectclass=user)(objectcategory=user)(userPrincipalName=&lt;username&gt;*))'</i> or for OpenLDAP: <i>'(&(objectClass=account)(uid=&lt;username&gt))'</i>.  '&lt;username&gt' is replaced with the username that was supplied at the login prompt. "
msgstr "Matacin bincike da za a yi amfani da shi don gano mai amfani a cikin kundin adireshi na LDAP, kamar na Windows: <i>'(&amp;(objectclass=user)(objectcategory=user)(userPrincipalName=&lt;username&gt;*))'</i> ko na OpenLDAP: <i>'(&(objectClass=account)(uid=&lt;username&gt))'</i>. Ana maye gurbin '&lt;username&gt' da sunan mai amfani da aka bayar a wurin shiga. "

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Search Distinguished Name (DN)"
msgstr "Keɓaɓɓen Suna (DN) na Bincike"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Distinguished Name for Specific Searching binding to the LDAP directory."
msgstr "Keɓaɓɓen Suna don Haɗin Bincike na Musamman zuwa kundin adireshin LDAP."

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
